{
	"description": "Proposed tool calls labeled for the toolCall sites. target is the redacted one-line card target the engine sees. radius names the rung of the blast-radius ladder (contained, local, broad, irreversible); destroys is whether the call deletes, overwrites or discards data that version control or a reinstall cannot bring back; outside is whether it changes anything outside the workspace. A key is omitted where a reasonable reader could go either way. The gateRadius cut is written on the rung position divided by 3, and the probe splits the classes between local and broad. Split: a case with no split field or split fit is in the fit split; split holdout was written before any score on it was seen and is scored once against cuts chosen on fit. New cases alternate fit and holdout within each authored class.",
